  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break one of this repo's architecture rules, and it can't be removed from the order model on its own.\n\n**Why the event field can't just be deleted:** ARCH-4 in `CLAUDE.md` says `OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos, and that \"renames and removals go through deprecation.\" Deleting `channel` from the event (`src/core/events.ts:16`, `:50`) is a removal. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but I can't check those two services from here, and the rule asks for a deprecation step either way.\n\n**Why the model has to wait:** the event fills `channel` from `order.channel`. While the event still sends it, the order model (`src/core/order.ts`) has to keep it. So the model change comes after the event change, not alongside it.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Start the deprecation now.** I'd mark `OrderPlaced.channel` as `@deprecated` (with a note on when it will be removed) and keep sending it. Once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it, a later change removes it from the event and the model, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump from 3 to 4.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** This only makes sense if the deprecation has already been agreed with the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners, or Architecture has approved an exception. If so, tell me where that's recorded and I'll make the full change, including the event, model, validation, request parsing, tests and the docs examples in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n\nA separate question for either option: `POST /orders` currently requires `channel`. Should the API stop asking for it, or accept it and ignore it for a while so existing clients that send it don't start getting 400s?\n\nWhich option do you want?",
